# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""037.md batch U: deepen vv 67, 119, 122, 132.

All four bodies were verified correct against their own verses before rewriting,
so this is depth work only.

vv 119, 122 and 132 are formula verses whose apparatus is a bare pointer (see
37:81c; see 37:77-79c), and their existing bodies said nearly the same thing
about the refrain's recurrence. Each is therefore written on a different angle:

  v119 the blessing left upon a PAIR -- the only one of the sūrah's four
       blessings given to two people at once -- and its placement at the end of
       the sequence of gifts.
  v122 the refrain in the PLURAL ("they were"), which is what makes the joint
       mission the thing characterised rather than either brother.
  v132 the refrain closing the Elias account, the shortest of the sūrah's
       prophetic narratives, and what its brevity does to the formula.

  v67  the boiling brew as a second stage, its parallel list, and the contrast
       with the drinks of the Garden. v66 already covers the eating and v68 the
       return to Hellfire, so neither is repeated.

Guards: no verbatim re-quote of the verse in the opening prose; no verbatim
repeat of blockquote wording in the prose above it; echo the verse's own
distinctive vocabulary; paragraphs distinct so duprate stays under 0.025.
"""

SURAH = "al-Ṣaffāt"
